This was it, if anyone wants it. Worked fine for my SNAPP runs. It's actually a super easy fix, I just removed line 65 in the function where the dataframe was sorted by population. There is no reason this actually needs to be sorted by population for snapp, so it works fine without it. The population assignments within beauti are exactly the same amount of work whether it's sorted by population or not.

